the link reader is a powerful tool for  language learners  make sure to take advantage of the  settings and personalize your reader  here's how i personalized mine  i don't want to turn my blue words  yellow when i click away from them or  make them known when i page  so i uncheck these settings  that way when i initially listen to the  audio and read through my lesson the  blue words won't change  once i'm ready to deal with my blue  words i can turn these settings back on  i also change the font and page size to  the way i like it  another way to get more out of link is  by tagging words and phrases  i can use the tag adjective or future  for the verb tense for example  how you tag is up to you  but you can start to tag based on which  vocabulary you want to focus on or are  having trouble with  once links are tagged i can review them  at any time in the vocabulary section  i just choose the tag or tags and up  comes the list of tagged terms which i  can then review  it's a good idea to tag words but also  phrases that encompass the concept you  are focusing on  if at any time i have a question about a  word or phrase in the lesson i just  click ask a tutor here and post my  question  i'll then be notified when a tutor gets  back to me  finally it's a great idea to take the  time to learn the keyboard shortcuts  i access them here and click show more  to see the full list  everyone has a preferred way of using  the reader and knowing the keyboard  shortcuts gives me the chance to figure  out mine  there are some special keys that help me  do some special tasks but mostly it's  the standard functions that are  convenient  for example i use the up down keys to  select different translations or known  and ignore  then right arrow to choose the current  selection and move on to the next  highlighted word  next time you're in the link reader  explore the different ways you can make  it work for you happy linking
 

